# SABOTAGE: P18 — THE LOGIN LANDING NEVER CONSULTS THE OPERATOR SEAT
# An operator who signs in with no `return_to` (a bookmark, a fresh tab, the invite-accept
# page's "sign in now" link) is supposed to land on the operator console — all tenant accounts,
# plans and MRR — because that is the surface their job starts on. This patch is that wiring
# REVERTED as if it had never been added: the seat branch, its `:roster` provenance check and
# its resolver are gone, so `landing/3` is just `safe_return/2` and every sign-in falls through
# to the host's `:tenant_landing`. Nothing errors, nothing logs; the operator simply arrives on a
# tenant dashboard and has to find the console in the sidebar.
#
# Two behaviors ride on the same branch, so both regress: the ARMED operator no longer reaches
# the console, and the dev-only rule (`Authz.seat_provenance/1` == :roster) disappears with it —
# re-wiring the seat WITHOUT that check is the exact mistake this shape reverts to, where a
# disarmed host's blanket `:operator_admin` sends every developer to the console.
#
# Why the dead code goes WITH the branch: leaving `operator_landing_seat?/2` (or its aliases)
# behind would fail the build on an unused-function/unused-alias warning, and a COMPILE failure
# is not a refutation — the tests have to run and fail. So the patch is a clean revert.
#
# Deliberately discriminating: the tenant CONTROLs, the `return_to`-wins test, the DISARMED twin
# and the open-redirect REDs all stay green (they assert unchanged behavior); only the three
# assertions about where an ARMED operator lands flip.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/login_landing_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: GREEN: an operator login with no return_to lands on the operator console
# MUST_FAIL: GREEN: the seat is resolved from the principal THIS login minted
# MUST_FAIL: RED: a protocol-relative return_to is dropped, then the operator landing applies
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/auth/session_controller.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/auth/session_controller.ex
@@ -111,9 +111,7 @@
   alias Samen.Web.Auth
   alias Samen.Web.Auth.Totp
   alias Samen.Web.Auth.TotpStepUp
-  alias Samen.Web.CurrentOrg
   alias Samen.Web.Mount
-  alias Samen.Web.Operator.Authz, as: OperatorAuthz
   alias Samen.Web.RateLimit
 
   @default_return "/"
@@ -790,21 +788,10 @@
   defp landing(conn, return_to, mount) do
     case sanitized_return(return_to) do
       {:ok, path} -> path
-      :none ->
-        if operator_landing_seat?(conn, mount),
-          do: CurrentOrg.operator_console_path(),
-          else: default_return(mount)
+      :none -> default_return(mount)
     end
   end
 
-  defp operator_landing_seat?(conn, mount) do
-    OperatorAuthz.seat_provenance(mount) == :roster and
-      not is_nil(OperatorAuthz.seat_role(mount, get_session(conn)))
-  rescue
-    # A host seam that raises must not fail a SUCCESSFUL login — fall back to the tenant
-    # landing (the pre-P18 behavior), never to the operator console.
-    _ -> false
-  end
 
   defp default_return(mount), do: Mount.label(mount, :tenant_landing, @default_return)
 end
